      "claim": "Because protection had lawfully ceased, the strike on 13 August 2025 was a lawful attack on a legitimate military objective and did not violate the protection owed to civilian medical units.",
      "reasoning": "Once the conditions of Article 19 GC IV and Article 13 AP I are met, the medical facility loses its special protection and may be targeted like any other military objective, provided the principles of distinction and precaution are respected. The attack was directed at the roof and top floor—where the observation team, machine‑gun and ammunition were located—and employed guided munitions specifically chosen to avoid the lower floors, demonstrating feasible precautions to minimize incidental harm. No civilians remained in the building after 12 August, satisfying the requirement that attacks not cause excessive civilian harm. Therefore, the strike complied with IHL and did not constitute a violation.",
