      "reasoning": "Article 19 of the Fourth Geneva Convention expressly states that protection does not cease unless a civilian hospital is used for acts harmful to the enemy. The occupation of the top floor as an artillery observation post, the firing of a heavy machine gun from the roof, and the storage of artillery ammunition in the basement are clearly acts of combat outside any humanitarian function. These uses are not among the exceptions listed in Additional Protocol I, which only exclude light personal defence weapons, pickets, small arms taken from the wounded, and the presence of combatants for medical reasons. Consequently, the hospital lost its protected status before the attack.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "treaty",
          "instrument": "gc_iv",
