      "reasoning": "Both Article 19 of the Fourth Geneva Convention and Article 13 of Additional Protocol I require that a warning be given, specifying a reasonable time‑limit, and that protection only cease after the warning remains unheeded. On 9 August Calvaran issued a radio broadcast, distributed leaflets, and delivered an ICRC delegate warning that military use must cease within 48 hours. The Drennick forces continued to use the hospital for observation and fire on 10 and 11 August, thereby ignoring the warning. The 48‑hour period elapsed unheeded, satisfying the statutory conditions for the cessation of protection.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "treaty",
          "instrument": "gc_iv",
