    {
      "claim": "The 13 August strike was directed at a legitimate military objective and complied with the principles of distinction and proportionality.",
      "reasoning": "After protection ceased, the top floor and roof of the building remained a functioning artillery observation post and firing position, qualifying as a military objective under customary IHL. The use of guided munitions aimed at the occupied floors, while deliberately avoiding the lower levels where civilians could have been present, demonstrates adherence to the distinction requirement. No civilians were in the building at the time of the attack, and the anticipated collateral damage was limited to the two enemy combatants, satisfying proportionality.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "type": "treaty",
          "instrument": "gc_iv",
          "article": "18",
          "quoted_text": "Civilian hospitals ... may in no circumstances be the object of attack, but shall at all times be respected and protected by the Parties to the conflict."
        },
        {
